  "answer": "",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "a | b means b = a·(some integer). Do the same for c, with a different new letter.",
    "Factor a out of b + c."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Since $a \\mid b$ and $a \\mid c$, $b = aj$ and $c = ak$ for some integers $j, k$.",
    "$b + c = aj + ak = a(j + k)$, and $j + k$ is an integer, so $a \\mid (b + c)$. $\\blacksquare$"
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "hammack-bop3",
    "section": "Chapter 4 exercises, #6 (p. 126)",
    "note": "This exact exercise, restated in ProofLab's words. Uses Definition 4.4 (divides)."
  },
